1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:03,676
Night of May 18, 1951,

2
00:00:03,687 --> 00:00:08,646
Yangpyeong, Gyeonggi Province.

3
00:00:08,496 --> 00:00:11,050
Mount Yongmun.

4
00:00:11,320 --> 00:00:16,970
At the headquarters of the Chinese

5
00:00:16,820 --> 00:00:21,823
63rd Army there was no doubt.

6
00:00:22,093 --> 00:00:26,361
"The enemy ahead is the same

7
00:00:26,211 --> 00:00:31,655
division we shattered a month ago."

8
00:00:31,925 --> 00:00:35,148
They were not wrong.

9
00:00:35,152 --> 00:00:38,946
Just one month earlier,

10
00:00:38,796 --> 00:00:45,124
at Sachang-ri the ROK 6th Division had

11
00:00:44,974 --> 00:00:50,669
collapsed under a Chinese assault.

12
00:00:50,939 --> 00:00:55,301
It abandoned its equipment,

13
00:00:55,151 --> 00:01:01,542
fled over the mountains, and scattered.

14
00:01:01,812 --> 00:01:05,583
So the Chinese committed

15
00:01:05,433 --> 00:01:09,354
three divisions at once.

16
00:01:09,355 --> 00:01:13,880
Three divisions, against one.

17
00:01:14,149 --> 00:01:19,004
On paper it was a battle that

18
00:01:18,854 --> 00:01:24,358
would be over in a single night.

19
00:01:24,778 --> 00:01:27,819
Yet ten days later,

20
00:01:27,821 --> 00:01:33,904
it was the Chinese who were on the run.

21
00:01:34,175 --> 00:01:38,784
And at the end of that road

22
00:01:38,634 --> 00:01:42,913
a vast lake was waiting.

23
00:01:43,183 --> 00:01:47,257
This is the story of how a

24
00:01:47,107 --> 00:01:51,182
defeated army rose again.

25
00:01:51,183 --> 00:01:56,675
And how one lake came to be called

26
00:01:56,525 --> 00:02:02,804
'The Lake That Defeated the Invaders.'

27
00:02:03,074 --> 00:02:05,186
Spring, 1951.

28
00:02:05,187 --> 00:02:10,168
The Chinese launched what became

29
00:02:10,018 --> 00:02:14,848
known as the Spring Offensive.

30
00:02:15,117 --> 00:02:19,845
The first phase came in April.

31
00:02:19,695 --> 00:02:23,508
The second, in mid-May.

32
00:02:23,778 --> 00:02:27,524
The objective was clear.

33
00:02:27,524 --> 00:02:31,270
Drive the United Nations

34
00:02:31,120 --> 00:02:35,166
forces off the peninsula.

35
00:02:35,166 --> 00:02:40,110
At the very least, retake Seoul.

36
00:02:40,381 --> 00:02:45,472
The ROK 6th Division was attached

37
00:02:45,322 --> 00:02:49,214
to the U.S. Ninth Corps.

38
00:02:49,214 --> 00:02:54,155
Its sector: north of Yangpyeong,

39
00:02:54,005 --> 00:02:57,449
around Mount Yongmun.

40
00:02:57,718 --> 00:03:01,839
A rugged peak rising eleven

41
00:03:01,689 --> 00:03:06,544
hundred and fifty-seven meters.

42
00:03:06,815 --> 00:03:10,789
The division commander was

43
00:03:10,639 --> 00:03:15,641
Brigadier General Chang Do-yong.

44
00:03:15,639 --> 00:03:19,759
He used this terrain to set

45
00:03:19,609 --> 00:03:23,583
up an unusual deployment.

46
00:03:23,852 --> 00:03:29,216
Forward, he placed a single unit,

47
00:03:29,066 --> 00:03:34,431
the 2nd Regiment, as an outpost.

48
00:03:34,439 --> 00:03:41,225
Behind it, on the main line of resistance,

49
00:03:41,075 --> 00:03:45,649
the 7th and 19th Regiments.

50
00:03:45,919 --> 00:03:51,216
A forward outpost exists to warn of

51
00:03:51,066 --> 00:03:56,804
the enemy's approach and to buy time.

52
00:03:56,801 --> 00:04:03,275
It is not meant to fight a decisive battle.

53
00:04:03,545 --> 00:04:07,240
On the other side stood

54
00:04:07,090 --> 00:04:10,784
the Chinese 63rd Army.

55
00:04:10,789 --> 00:04:16,795
The 187th, 188th, and 189th Divisions.

56
00:04:17,065 --> 00:04:20,570
Their plan was simple.

57
00:04:20,573 --> 00:04:23,773
Infiltrate by night,

58
00:04:23,623 --> 00:04:28,348
encircle, and break the line.

59
00:04:28,351 --> 00:04:33,991
Just as they had done at Sachang-ri.

60
00:04:34,262 --> 00:04:40,147
But the Chinese did not know one thing.

61
00:04:40,144 --> 00:04:45,588
What the men of the 6th Division had

62
00:04:45,438 --> 00:04:50,736
sworn to themselves in that month.

63
00:04:51,005 --> 00:04:54,390
The night of May 18th.

64
00:04:54,387 --> 00:04:58,214
The Chinese attack began.

65
00:04:58,484 --> 00:05:03,904
Bugles sounded in the darkness

66
00:05:03,914 --> 00:05:08,695
and hundreds, then thousands,

67
00:05:08,545 --> 00:05:12,528
climbed the ridgelines.

68
00:05:12,798 --> 00:05:18,830
They ran straight into the 2nd Regiment.

69
00:05:18,827 --> 00:05:21,919
The forward outpost.

70
00:05:22,189 --> 00:05:27,192
And here came the first reversal.

71
00:05:27,462 --> 00:05:32,759
The 2nd Regiment did not fall back.

72
00:05:33,029 --> 00:05:39,348
Under wave after wave of attacks, the 2nd

73
00:05:39,198 --> 00:05:46,420
Regiment was quickly encircled on three sides.

74
00:05:46,690 --> 00:05:52,178
With communications barely holding,

75
00:05:52,028 --> 00:05:58,431
Colonel Song Dae-hoo and his men refused

76
00:05:58,281 --> 00:06:03,616
to yield, and fought to the last.

77
00:06:03,886 --> 00:06:09,938
In response, U.S. Ninth Corps artillery

78
00:06:09,788 --> 00:06:14,629
and supporting units laid down

79
00:06:14,479 --> 00:06:18,563
an unprecedented barrage,

80
00:06:18,413 --> 00:06:24,919
right in front of the friendly positions,

81
00:06:24,920 --> 00:06:29,912
and the northern ridges of Mount

82
00:06:29,762 --> 00:06:35,965
Yongmun were pounded through the night.

83
00:06:36,236 --> 00:06:40,563
This was a unit expected to

84
00:06:40,413 --> 00:06:45,049
hold briefly, then withdraw.

85
00:06:45,054 --> 00:06:50,928
But the 2nd Regiment held its ground.

86
00:06:50,932 --> 00:06:54,872
Surrounded, running low

87
00:06:54,722 --> 00:06:58,662
on ammunition it held.

88
00:06:58,932 --> 00:07:03,023
And so the Chinese command

89
00:07:02,873 --> 00:07:06,963
made a fatal misjudgment.

90
00:07:06,965 --> 00:07:11,270
"They're holding this hard

91
00:07:11,120 --> 00:07:15,906
this must be the main line."

92
00:07:16,176 --> 00:07:20,738
The Chinese kept pouring three

93
00:07:20,588 --> 00:07:26,620
divisions into this one small position.

94
00:07:26,890 --> 00:07:31,754
May 19th, and on into the 20th.

95
00:07:31,756 --> 00:07:37,532
Each night they surged in like waves.

96
00:07:37,382 --> 00:07:45,287
Each dawn they fell back, leaving only their dead.

97
00:07:45,557 --> 00:07:50,560
The 6th Division's records report

98
00:07:50,410 --> 00:07:54,531
the slopes in front of the

99
00:07:54,381 --> 00:07:59,825
position covered with Chinese dead.

100
00:08:00,095 --> 00:08:05,583
And behind that position American

101
00:08:05,433 --> 00:08:10,598
artillery fired without pause.

102
00:08:10,868 --> 00:08:12,723
Three days.

103
00:08:12,728 --> 00:08:19,235
For the three days the 2nd Regiment held,

104
00:08:19,085 --> 00:08:24,041
the Chinese were wearing down.

105
00:08:24,046 --> 00:08:27,811
Out of rations, out of

106
00:08:27,661 --> 00:08:32,412
ammunition and out of time.

107
00:08:32,832 --> 00:08:35,776
Then came May 21st.

108
00:08:35,773 --> 00:08:38,864
The 6th Division was

109
00:08:38,714 --> 00:08:42,688
ordered to counterattack.

110
00:08:42,958 --> 00:08:47,289
The 7th and 19th Regiments,

111
00:08:47,139 --> 00:08:51,315
waiting on the main line,

112
00:08:51,320 --> 00:08:55,032
moved forward together.

113
00:08:55,301 --> 00:08:57,753
In that moment,

114
00:08:57,603 --> 00:09:02,663
the attacker became the hunted.

115
00:09:02,933 --> 00:09:08,677
The exhausted Chinese began to break.

116
00:09:08,678 --> 00:09:13,818
The retreat soon became a rout

117
00:09:13,819 --> 00:09:17,749
and the 6th Division gave

118
00:09:17,599 --> 00:09:21,377
chase without stopping.

119
00:09:21,647 --> 00:09:25,580
Past Gapyeong, along the

120
00:09:25,430 --> 00:09:29,521
Bukhan River, northward.

121
00:09:29,529 --> 00:09:34,185
And at the end of that road

122
00:09:34,035 --> 00:09:38,191
the Hwacheon Reservoir.

123
00:09:38,461 --> 00:09:43,399
Cut off, the Chinese forces were

124
00:09:43,249 --> 00:09:47,588
driven to the water's edge.

125
00:09:47,588 --> 00:09:51,927
Deep water ahead. ROK and UN

126
00:09:51,777 --> 00:09:56,117
forces closing from behind.

127
00:09:56,387 --> 00:10:00,366
Many fell here, drowned,

128
00:10:00,216 --> 00:10:04,196
or were taken prisoner.

129
00:10:04,466 --> 00:10:09,979
Pushing north to retake the Hwacheon

130
00:10:09,829 --> 00:10:16,237
power plant and dam, the ROK 6th Division

131
00:10:16,087 --> 00:10:22,345
pressed in from all sides on the Chinese

132
00:10:22,195 --> 00:10:27,857
troops trapped around the reservoir.

133
00:10:28,127 --> 00:10:33,687
Blocked by rugged mountains and cold

134
00:10:33,537 --> 00:10:38,196
water, the retreating enemy's

135
00:10:38,046 --> 00:10:43,907
command structure collapsed entirely,

136
00:10:43,907 --> 00:10:49,768
and the Hwacheon area became the final

137
00:10:49,618 --> 00:10:56,230
graveyard of the Chinese Spring Offensive.

138
00:10:56,500 --> 00:11:01,185
Years later, President Syngman

139
00:11:01,035 --> 00:11:06,022
Rhee gave this lake a new name.

140
00:11:06,024 --> 00:11:07,685
Lake Paro.

141
00:11:07,955 --> 00:11:11,263
Pa, to destroy. Ro,

142
00:11:11,113 --> 00:11:15,917
the invaders. Ho, the lake.

143
00:11:16,187 --> 00:11:20,880
The division defeated just a

144
00:11:20,730 --> 00:11:26,396
month earlier had renamed a lake.

145
00:11:26,666 --> 00:11:32,551
So how did one division hold off three?

146
00:11:32,548 --> 00:11:38,287
Let's break it down into four factors.

147
00:11:38,556 --> 00:11:45,477
First, the deception of the forward outpost.

148
00:11:45,747 --> 00:11:50,841
Because the 2nd Regiment held far

149
00:11:50,691 --> 00:11:55,935
longer than expected, the Chinese

150
00:11:55,785 --> 00:12:01,928
misjudged the main axis of the defense.

151
00:12:01,928 --> 00:12:07,771
With their forces massed in one place,

152
00:12:07,621 --> 00:12:13,315
the two regiments behind it prepared

153
00:12:13,165 --> 00:12:18,409
a counterattack almost untouched.

154
00:12:18,679 --> 00:12:24,329
Intended or not this was the first

155
00:12:24,179 --> 00:12:29,182
move that decided the battle.

156
00:12:29,452 --> 00:12:32,549
Second, firepower.

157
00:12:32,819 --> 00:12:37,008
The Chinese relied on mass,

158
00:12:36,858 --> 00:12:40,897
the so-called human wave.

159
00:12:40,896 --> 00:12:45,384
Behind the 6th Division stood

160
00:12:45,234 --> 00:12:50,769
American artillery and air support.

161
00:12:51,039 --> 00:12:58,130
And the denser the waves climbing the slopes

162
00:12:57,980 --> 00:13:05,071
the heavier the toll the shells would take.

163
00:13:05,341 --> 00:13:07,850
Third, supply.

164
00:13:08,120 --> 00:13:14,299
Chinese soldiers fought with the food and

165
00:13:14,149 --> 00:13:20,182
ammunition they carried on their backs.

166
00:13:20,179 --> 00:13:25,770
That was enough for roughly one week.

167
00:13:26,040 --> 00:13:29,805
UN forces called it 'the

168
00:13:29,655 --> 00:13:32,968
one-week offensive.'

169
00:13:32,969 --> 00:13:38,098
By the time the 2nd Regiment had

170
00:13:37,948 --> 00:13:43,077
held for three days the Chinese

171
00:13:42,927 --> 00:13:47,278
clock had all but run out.

172
00:13:47,548 --> 00:13:51,832
Fourth, terrain and morale.

173
00:13:51,835 --> 00:13:57,345
Rising above eleven hundred meters,

174
00:13:57,195 --> 00:14:02,857
Mount Yongmun favored the defender.

175
00:14:03,127 --> 00:14:08,144
And above all the 6th Division

176
00:14:07,994 --> 00:14:13,336
carried the scar of Sachang-ri.

177
00:14:13,341 --> 00:14:19,371
The memory of that defeat, and the vow

178
00:14:19,221 --> 00:14:25,406
never to retreat again, held the line.

179
00:14:25,676 --> 00:14:31,509
Official South Korean histories credit

180
00:14:31,359 --> 00:14:36,444
this series of battles with more

181
00:14:36,294 --> 00:14:41,229
than seventeen thousand Chinese

182
00:14:41,079 --> 00:14:47,062
killed and over two thousand captured.

183
00:14:47,061 --> 00:14:51,785
The 6th Division's own losses

184
00:14:51,635 --> 00:14:55,885
numbered in the hundreds.

185
00:14:56,155 --> 00:15:00,182
Of course, wartime figures

186
00:15:00,032 --> 00:15:04,208
are prone to exaggeration.

187
00:15:04,207 --> 00:15:08,831
Claims that 'tens of thousands

188
00:15:08,681 --> 00:15:13,900
drowned' at Lake Paro are treated

189
00:15:13,750 --> 00:15:18,076
with caution by historians.

190
00:15:18,346 --> 00:15:21,919
But one fact is clear.

191
00:15:21,924 --> 00:15:28,084
After this battle, the Chinese Spring

192
00:15:27,934 --> 00:15:33,120
Offensive could go no further.

193
00:15:33,389 --> 00:15:37,565
Today, Lake Paro is quiet.

194
00:15:37,570 --> 00:15:40,817
Fishing boats drift,

195
00:15:40,667 --> 00:15:45,463
and mist rises off the water.

196
00:15:45,733 --> 00:15:49,702
But beneath that water

197
00:15:49,704 --> 00:15:54,589
lie the lost years of countless

198
00:15:54,439 --> 00:15:59,324
young men who never came home.

199
00:15:59,594 --> 00:16:04,303
The men of the 2nd Regiment who

200
00:16:04,153 --> 00:16:09,303
held the ridges of Mount Yongmun.

201
00:16:09,300 --> 00:16:15,626
Most of them were around twenty years old.

202
00:16:15,623 --> 00:16:19,597
Ordinary young men who had

203
00:16:19,447 --> 00:16:23,715
left their parents at home.

204
00:16:23,985 --> 00:16:28,220
And the Chinese soldiers

205
00:16:28,070 --> 00:16:31,794
who fell by the lake

206
00:16:31,803 --> 00:16:35,783
were, for the most part,

207
00:16:35,633 --> 00:16:42,006
young men too, sent to a foreign land.

208
00:16:42,425 --> 00:16:47,921
The lesson of Yongmunsan is simple.

209
00:16:47,923 --> 00:16:51,739
A single defeat does not

210
00:16:51,589 --> 00:16:56,015
decide the fate of an army.

211
00:16:56,018 --> 00:17:00,544
And in war, the real weapon

212
00:17:00,394 --> 00:17:04,110
is not numbers alone.

213
00:17:04,381 --> 00:17:08,992
In one month, from a defeated

214
00:17:08,842 --> 00:17:13,607
division to a victorious one.

215
00:17:13,611 --> 00:17:18,142
And in between were the men

216
00:17:17,992 --> 00:17:22,684
who decided to stand again.

217
00:17:23,104 --> 00:17:28,776
If this story meant something to you,

218
00:17:28,626 --> 00:17:34,298
please subscribe and like the video.

219
00:17:34,298 --> 00:17:38,477
We'll continue to bring the

220
00:17:38,327 --> 00:17:43,701
forgotten records of war to light.
